<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Land of Lebus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lubusz Land</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebou-people">Lebus</a> is a historical region on both banks of the middle Oder around the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebus">Lebus</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Held by the Piast dukes of Poland and Silesia, it was taken by the margraves of Brandenburg around 1250 and became part of the Brandenburg march.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/land-of-lebus.jpg" alt="Land of Lebus" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TomaszPrzezdziecki · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%81ag%C3%B3w_Lubuski_aerial_2023_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
